# 6️⃣ Flood Fill

## Problem

Replace connected cells having:

```text
Old Color
```

with:

```text
New Color
```

---

### Example

```text
1 1 1

1 1 0

1 0 1
```

Change:

```text
1 → 2
```

Result:

```text
2 2 2

2 2 0

2 0 1
```

---

# 7️⃣ DFS Solution

```cpp
void floodFill(
    int row,
    int col,
    int initialColor,
    int newColor,
    vector<vector<int>>& image)
{
    image[row][col] =
        newColor;

    int dr[] =
    {-1,0,1,0};

    int dc[] =
    {0,1,0,-1};

    for(int i=0;i<4;i++)
    {
        int nr =
            row + dr[i];

        int nc =
            col + dc[i];

        if(
            nr>=0 &&
            nc>=0 &&
            nr<image.size() &&
            nc<image[0].size() &&
            image[nr][nc]
            ==
            initialColor
        )
        {
            floodFill(
                nr,
                nc,
                initialColor,
                newColor,
                image
            );
        }
    }
}
```

